A thread that joins a ring is not linked from the newest thread before it.
A signal or a switch would never reach it, and the ring would not close;
a queue is a ring linked both ways.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a waiting or ready thread is on no queue
Report: queue is not linked back

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ static void ring_push(paddr_t *head, struct thread *t)
         struct thread *newest = p2v(oldest->queue_prev);
         t->queue_next = *head;
         t->queue_prev = oldest->queue_prev;
-        newest->queue_next = self;
+        (void)newest;
         oldest->queue_prev = self;
     }
 }
